{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And it shall be there for you as a witness.</b> It will testify that I knew you would forsake the Torah of the blessed El — for whose sake I needed to place one scroll of the Torah in a place where no one enters except the High Priest once a year. And this scroll will testify that everything found written in the scroll of the Torah that will be found in the hands of the righteous of the generation — these are the very words spoken to Moses from Sinai, without addition or subtraction, and thereby no doubt will arise in you concerning them. However, the scroll that Hilkiah found (II Kings 22:8) appears to have been the scroll that Moses gave to the priests, the bearers of the ark of the covenant of YHWH, mentioned above (Deuteronomy 31:9) — which contained only the section of the king, and in it Joshua wrote the covenant that he renewed with Israel in recompense for what they accepted upon themselves therein: to serve the exalted El in truth and wholeness — which is in both thought and deed. And when Josiah read it and saw that they had distanced themselves from all this, he trembled and inquired of YHWH concerning this matter."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:52.332806644Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}